response:
To terminate a C program, you can use the `exit()` function. This function is part of the C standard library and is used to terminate the program and return a status code to the operating system. Here's an example of how to use the `exit()` function:

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

int main() {
    printf("Hello, world!\n");
    exit(0);  // Terminate the program with status code 0
    return 0;  // Return 0 to indicate successful termination
}
```

In this example, the program prints "Hello, world!"
